  "summary_en": "Section 1a of the German Road Traffic Act permits operation of motor vehicles with automated driving functions when used as intended. It sets technical requirements (manual override, handover warnings, misuse alerts), manufacturer declaration duties, type-approval conditions, and defines the person activating the function as the driver.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Operation with automated driving function is lawful if used as intended",
   "Systems must be manually overridable or deactivatable at any time",
   "System must signal need for manual control with sufficient time reserve",
   "Manufacturer must bindingly declare conformity in the system description",
   "Person activating the function remains the vehicle driver"
  ],
